procedure test_FieldOfDefinition()
    QQ := Rationals();
    _<x> := PolynomialRing(QQ);
    // SOURCE OF TRUTH: [GY] = J.-W. Guo, Y. Yang, "Equations of hyperelliptic Shimura curves",
    // arXiv:1510.06193 v1, Appendix B.  EVERY VALUE BELOW IS FROM arXiv v1, which is the only arXiv
    // version; the paper of record (Compositio Math. 153 (2017) 1-40) is substantially revised and
    // is not on arXiv, so some misprints noted below may be corrected there.  Table numbers are the
    // arXiv v1 numbering: CM-value tables 9-50, equation tables 2-8.  Each CM-value table gives, per
    // CM discriminant, the coordinate on the star quotient and on one or two proper subquotients;
    // the expected field K below is the field generated by that coordinate.
    //
    // Provenance of the expected values.  Every entry was re-checked against arXiv v1 on 2026-09-24.
    //  (a) STRAIGHT FROM [GY]: every entry not listed in (b)-(c).  Where [GY] prints a nested
    //      radical, K is the field it generates (e.g. sqrt(1+4sqrt(-3)) = 2+sqrt(-3)); those
    //      simplifications are noted inline and were checked by squaring.
    //  (b) CORRECTED BY SOLVING [GY]'S OWN EQUATIONS (the printed coordinate contradicts the
    //      printed parameter or relation; K is what the relation forces):
    //        (39,1,<w39>)   d=-123   Table 12: s=1/5 in s=(2x^2-3x-2)/x gives 5x^2-8x-5=0, so
    //                                 x=(4+-sqrt(41))/5, not (4+-sqrt(11))/5.
    //        (57,1,<w19>)  all       Table 15 labels BOTH columns W_{57,1}; Table 2 gives
    //                                 x^2=-4s^2+2s-1 with w19(s,x,y)=(s,x,-y), so the x column is
    //                                 X/<w19>.  Every printed x satisfies that relation.
    //        (57,1,<w19>)  d=-4      Table 15 prints x=oo at s=oo; x^2=-4s^2+... gives
    //                                 x/s=+-2sqrt(-1), so K=Q(sqrt(-1)).
    //        (82,1,<w41>)  d=-19     Table 20 prints x=oo; Table 3's x^2=-19s^2+18s-11 at s=oo
    //                                 gives K=Q(sqrt(-19)).
    //        (86,1,<w86>)  d=-228    Table 21 prints +-sqrt(19)+-2sqrt(-3); x^2=9-4s with
    //                                 s=10+-sqrt(57) needs (sqrt(-19)+2sqrt(-3))^2=-31+4sqrt(57).
    //        (93,1,<w31>)  d=-4      Table 23 prints x=oo; Table 3's x^2=-4s^2-6s-9 at s=oo
    //                                 gives K=Q(sqrt(-1)).
    //        (10,23,<w230>) d=-120   Table 42: t=5/sqrt(-3) in t=(5x^2+5)/(x^2-4x-1) gives
    //                                 discriminant -800/3, so K=Q(sqrt(-3),sqrt(2)).
    //        (21,2,<w3,w7>) d=-708   Table 46 prints +-5/(4sqrt(-3)) but s=x^2=25/48>0: K=Q(sqrt(3)).
    //        (39,2,<w39>)  d=-372    Table 50: t=5/sqrt(-3) in t=3(x^2+4x+2)/(x^2-2) gives
    //                                 discriminant 16/3, so K=Q(sqrt(-3),sqrt(-1)).
    //  (c) REFUTED BY SHIMURA RECIPROCITY APPLIED TO [GY]'S OWN EQUATIONS: (26,3,<w3,w26>)
    //      d=-267 and d=-708, Table 49.  The sign-flipped value is the unique consistent rational
    //      s of height <= 400 (searched in that block).  Tested in their own block at the end.
    //
    // REMOVED, NOT TESTED ("if you don't know, don't write the test"): rows where [GY] prints
    // something that is not a usable value and nothing in [GY] decides the fix.
    //    Table 30 (159,1): a row d=-57, which is not a discriminant (on both D=159 curves).
    //    Table 41 (10,19): d=-52 printed twice (s=oo and s=-4); one is some other discriminant.
    //        Dropped on <w5,w38> (which -52 row is real is unknown); d=-52 is kept on the star
    //        quotient only, where both rows give s in Q.
    //    Table 32 (206,1,<w206>) d=-132: only the DEGREE is tested (degree_only_pts).  [GY]'s field
    //        Q(sqrt(3),sqrt(11)) has degree 4, which is source-backed; the code's field is
    //        Q(sqrt(-3),sqrt(-11)).  Both lie in the ring class field, so nothing independent
    //        decides between them: the field disagreement is unresolved and not asserted.
    //
    // Not included: Tables 10 (D=35) and 45 (15,2), and the rows of Table 9 (D=26) below -67.
    //    They have been absent since the test was first written (d81d8e9); the reason was not
    //    recorded.  Probed on 2026-09-24 (not asserted here): every omitted row agrees with the code
    //    except Table 10 d=-1435, where [GY] prints x = +-3sqrt(-41)/7 on X_0^35(1)/<w35>.  That is
    //    a [GY] misprint: sqrt(-41) is not in the genus field Q(sqrt(5),sqrt(-7),sqrt(41)) of -1435,
    //    so not in H_R, and the printed s = -369/7 with s = x^2 gives x = +-3sqrt(-287)/7, i.e.
    //    Q(sqrt(-287)), which is what the code gives.

    // Field disputed with [GY], degree source-backed: the field assertions skip these.
    degree_only_pts := [<206, 1, {1,206}, -132>];
    data := [
        <26, 1, {1,2,13,26}, [* <-8, QQ>, <-11, QQ>, <-19, QQ>, <-20, QQ>, <-24, QQ>, <-52, QQ>, <-67, QQ> *] >,
